oceeding the same way is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; it denotes the relative motion only. Here the pass is read while under way - the bodies side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero; a projection, not a contact or a distance) after the rider was ahead within the window - and once completed, from the observation at which the concept rises, within the window."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle, 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each admitted aggregate claimed whole."}, {"span": "b3", "atoms": ["rel.same_direction", "kin.speed"], "derived": [], "justification": "'proceeding' is the overtaken road user moving (kin.speed above the halt tolerance); 'in the same direction' is rel.same_direction ('headings aligned') between the subject and it."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a motor vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'). 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "st.lane_adjacency"], "derived": [], "justification": "'only one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction' is the count of lanes in the direction of a lane (st.lane) the overtaken rider occupies (rel.occupies) being the stated one (st.lane_adjacency, 'the count of lanes in that direction'). 'traffic' names the users of the lane; no membership is read."}, {"span": "b9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane", "rel.bearing"], "derived": ["drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier"], "justification": "'move again to the right side of the highway': having moved out to the left of the rider (rel.bearing from the subject, lateral component negative: the rider on its right), the subject turns back toward the side the rider keeps: drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier(subject, L) for a lane L (st.lane) the rider occupies (rel.occupies) - 'a, moving, points to the right of the designated direction of travel of carrier region r by more than a tolerance'. The concept says nothing of whether the subject occupies L, so it reads a move back toward the rider's lane from the opposing lane or from the left part of the rider's lane alike. 'again' fixes the order: the subject first had the rider on its right."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b10", "standard": "until the vehicle is safely clear of the overtaken bicycle", "concepts": ["rel.surface_gap", "rel.bearing", "rel.longitudinal_overlap", "kin.speed", "env.ice_or_snow", "env.wet_road", "env.precipitation"], "params": ["p.following_headway_dry", "p.following_headway_wet", "p.following_headway_ice"], "convention": "time headway: the subject (the vehicle) is safely clear of the overtaken rider where the rider is behind it (rel.bearing longitudinal component negative, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative) with a gap between the bodies (rel.surface_gap) of at least the rider's speed times the following headway for the surface - ice or snow, else wet road or precipitation, else dry - so that the rider, following, keeps the headway a following road user keeps", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_1", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2a", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2b", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2c", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_217_2", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}], "residues": [{"span": "b12", "why": "the authorization lets a driver passing a rider at the stated clearance pass left of the center or in a no-passing zone, conduct other rules (NRS 484B.213, 484B.217) forbid; it relaxes those rules and leaves the duty not to move back right before being clear unchanged", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. Some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) with its heading aligned with the subject's (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos), is being overtaken by the subject: at some observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window r was ahead of the subject (rel.bearing longitudinal component positive, rel.longitudinal_overlap negative) with aligned headings, and either r is not yet behind the subject or drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r) (window p.overtake_window, same_dir_cos p.overtake_same_direction_cos) has risen at some observation of that window; r lies on the subject's right (rel.bearing lateral component negative); and r occupies a st.lane whose count of lanes in its direction (st.lane_adjacency count) is the literal one.", "obligation": "For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection), where r is not safely clear behind the subject - that is, not (r behind the subject, rel.bearing longitudinal component negative and rel.longitudinal_overlap negative, with rel.surface_gap at least r's kin.speed times the headway: p.following_headway_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.following_headway_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.following_headway_dry) - the subject does not move to the right: drv.lane.heading_right_of_carrier(subject, L) with sin_tol p.course_departure_sin_tol and speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance holds for no st.lane L that r occupies (rel.occupies).", "params": ["p.overtake_window", "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.course_departure_sin_tol", "p.following_headway_dry", "p.following_headway_wet", "p.following_headway_ice"], "narrowings": [{"span": "b4", "why": "'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "b9", "why": "'move again to the right side of the highway' is read as the subject's heading turned to the right of the rider's lane direction beyond the course tolerance, after it has the rider on its right; a gradual drift within that tolerance is not read", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "b10", "why": "'safely clear' is read as the rider behind the subject at a time-headway gap at the rider's speed; the rider's own braking ability is not otherwise read", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Road with one lane in the subject's direction; the subject car moves out left and overtakes a bicycle; while the bicycle is still beside it, the subject car steers back to the right, its heading turning right of the lane's direction beyond the course tolerance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same pass; the subject car keeps its course until the bicycle is behind it at a gap above the bicycle's speed times the dry headway, then steers back right."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car overtakes another car on a one-lane road and steers back; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe headings.", "masked": ["kin.heading"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject car completes the pass of an electric scooter and steers back right at once, the scooter behind it at a gap below its speed times the dry headway."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The road has two lanes in the subject's direction; the subject passes a bicycle and steers back right while beside it."}], "literals": [{"span": "b6", "text": "one", "value": 1, "unit": "count"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-duration figures"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other", "source": "lane-change heading figures"}, {"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "source speed resolution"}, {"name": "p.course_departure_sin_tol", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.035, "convention": "sine of the largest angle (about two degrees) between a moving vehicle's heading and its lane's designated direction at which it counts as keeping its course: lane-keeping heading wander plus the source's heading noise, below the few degrees of heading a lane change takes", "source": "lane-keeping studies"}, {"name": "p.following_headway_dry", "unit": "s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "time headway a following driver keeps on a dry surface: the two-second rule of driver manuals", "source": "driver manuals"}, {"name": "p.following_headway_wet", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time headway a following driver keeps on a wet surface or in rain: the two-second rule lengthened by a second", "source": "driver manuals"}, {"name": "p.following_headway_ice", "unit": "s", "value": 6.0, "convention": "time headway a following driver keeps on an icy or snow-covered surface: the tripled following time driver manuals advise", "source": "driver manuals"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}

