{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_2_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-2"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "a", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b", "text": "or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "d", "text": "shall stop in obedience to a stop sign or yield in compliance with a yield sign,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "f", "text": "in compliance with the manner prescribed in subsection 1 [NRS-484B-257-1],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "g", "text": "prior to entering an intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "h", "text": "if a stop sign or a yield sign is erected at one or more entrances thereto", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "i", "text": "although not a part of a through highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "j", "text": "and shall proceed cautiously,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "k", "text": "yielding", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "l", "text": "to vehicles not so obligated to stop or yield", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "m", "text": "and which are within the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "n", "text": "or approaching so closely as to constitute an immediate hazard", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "o", "text": "during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "a", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, of which the subject is a member; 'being controlled by a police officer' is dev.human_direction of role police_officer ('a person directing traffic') governing (dev.governs) the subject's approach carrier c or X (st.travel_region), read at the subject's entry."}, {"span": "b", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal", "dev.governs", "dev.inoperative"], "derived": [], "justification": "A dev.traffic_signal governing c or X (dev.governs) that is not dev.inoperative ('installed and uncovered but showing no valid indication'), read at the subject's entry."}, {"span": "c", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "Same mapping as 'The driver of a vehicle' in the index: the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'driver' is the vehicle's controlled motion."}, {"span": "d", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "kin.speed", "st.stop_line", "st.crosswalk", "st.entrance_of", "prim.region_offset_along", "st.lane_direction", "st.region_geometry", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'Stop' is DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement' (drv.motion.complete_halt); 'in obedience to a stop sign' ties the halt to a dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') governing (dev.governs) the subject's approach carrier c or X. 'Yield in compliance with a yield sign' (dev.yield_sign, 'regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt'), in the manner subsection 1 prescribes ('in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped'), is the subject's kin.speed within the place's stopping zone at or below the speed from which it still halts at the place (p.yield_line_speed_max), a halt included. The act is owed at the place that manner names, which the act's own atoms read: the st.stop_line marking c (st.entrance_of), else the st.crosswalk marking c, else c's entrance end, the side along c's direction (st.lane_direction) given by prim.region_offset_along, the body-to-mark distance by st.region_geometry, the subject on c by rel.occupies."}, {"span": "g", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Prior to entering an intersection': the act is owed before the subject's entry into X - the observation at which its footprint comes to overlap X (rel.occupies), having occupied at the previous observation a carrier c entering X (st.lane_enters, st.travel_region)."}, {"span": "h", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A stop sign or a yield sign is erected at one or more entrances thereto': a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs (dev.governs) an approach carrier of X (st.lane_enters) or X; the sign the subject obeys is the one governing its own entrance c, which it occupies (rel.occupies)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "f", "rule": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [{"span": "i", "why": "'although' is concessive: the duty reaches signed entrances whether or not the intersection is part of a through highway, and the stop or yield owed at a signed entrance is the same in both cases (subsection 1 states the same act where it is part of one); the words withhold the duty nowhere.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "At the subject's entry into an intersection X: the observation at which its footprint overlaps X and did not at the previous observation, where at that previous observation it occupied a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, X); where at the entry observation a stop sign or a yield sign governs c or X (dev.governs); except where at that observation a police officer's direction (dev.human_direction of role police_officer) governs c or X, or a traffic signal that is not inoperative governs c or X.", "obligation": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1 (binder subject to subject) is complied with at the entry - the manner subsection 1 prescribes - and the act it states is found on the approach: where a stop sign governs c or X, a complete halt (drv.motion.complete_halt, speed_tol p.halt_speed_tolerance); where only a yield sign does, an observation at which kin.speed is at or below p.yield_line_speed_max (a halt included); in either case while occupying c within the stopping zone of the place for c, in subsection 1's order: (1) a stop line marking c's entrance (st.entrance_of), the line ahead of or at the reference point along c's direction (prim.region_offset_along at or above zero), the body within p.stop_point_tolerance of it; (2) where no stop line marks c (entrance lists observed and excluding c), the crosswalk marking c's entrance ahead, not overlapped, the body within p.stop_point_tolerance of it; (3) where neither marks c, the footprint outside X and the body within p.stop_point_tolerance of X. History bound: the search runs back from the entry and ends at the approach start - the last observation before the entry at which the subject, on a carrier the place marks, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream (off the mark, short of it along c's direction and farther than p.stop_point_tolerance; where several marks of that kind mark c, outside and short of each) - or at the subject's previous entry into X, whichever is later. Act found: compliant; either end reached without it: violated; neither end reached (the recording begins inside the zone): unknown. Each entry owes its own act; only an observed exit from the zone upstream begins a new approach. The entry is unknown where the previous observation does not show the subject on a mapped carrier; where a mark's association with c is unobserved and the verdict turns on it, unknown. No bound is taken from the recording's start, a first observation or a cumulative distance.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.stop_point_tolerance", "p.yield_line_speed_max"], "narrowings": [{"span": "c", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A dev.stop_sign governs carrier c entering X; a st.stop_line marks c; no officer or operating signal. The subject passes the line and enters X with kin.speed well above p.halt_speed_tolerance, never halting since it was upstream of the line's stopping zone."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same scene; the subject halts on c with the line just ahead within p.stop_point_tolerance, then enters X."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "No stop or yield sign governs c or X; the subject enters X without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "Stop sign governing c; kin.speed is absent, so whether the subject halted is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "Stop sign governing c; the recording begins with the subject already within p.stop_point_tolerance of the stop line, moving slowly; no halt is recorded before its entry into X.", "boundary": "the approach start: the subject's last observation outside the stop line's stopping zone upstream on c lies before the recording"}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Only a dev.yield_sign governs c; no stop line or crosswalk marks c; the subject reaches X's edge at kin.speed at or below p.yield_line_speed_max and enters."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A stop sign governs c, but an operating dev.traffic_signal (circular_red) also governs c at the subject's entry."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's kinematic channels"}, {"name": "p.stop_point_tolerance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin", "source": "MUTCD stop line placement in advance of a crosswalk"}, {"name": "p.yield_line_speed_max", "unit": "m/s", "value": 4.2, "convention": "the speed at or below which a vehicle at the place of a yield sign counts as having slowed: the speed from which a passenger car can still halt within the stop-point tolerance at a comfortable deceleration of about 4.5 m/s^2", "source": "AASHTO comfortable deceleration rate of the stopping sight distance model"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_267_2a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-267-2a"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "t1", "text": "Upon approaching", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "t2", "text": "an authorized emergency vehicle", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "t3", "text": "or an official vehicle of a regulatory agency", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "t4", "text": "which is moving or preparing to move in any direction,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "t5", "text": "including, without limitation, arriving at or leaving the scene of a crash or other incident,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "t6", "text": "and making use of flashing lights meeting the requirements of", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "t7", "text": "subsection 3 of NRS 484A.480 [DEF-NRS-484A-480-3],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "t8", "text": "the driver of any other vehicle shall,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "t9", "text": "except when otherwise directed by a law enforcement officer:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "t10", "text": "Decrease the speed of his or her vehicle", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "t11", "text": "to a speed that is reasonable and proper, pursuant to the criteria set forth in subsection 1 of NRS 484B.600 [NRS-484B-600-1a].", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "t12", "text": "As used in this section, “preparing to move” means any indication that is visible to an approaching driver that an authorized emergency vehicle or an official vehicle of a regulatory agency is about to move, including, without limitation: (a) A movement of the vehicle; or (b) The use of hand signals by the driver of the vehicle.", "role": "definitional"}], "elements": [{"span": "t1", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "rel.bearing", "rel.centre_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "'approaching' the emergency vehicle: the subject moves (kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' above the halt tolerance) with the emergency vehicle ahead of it in its own frame (rel.bearing 'direction of b from a in a's frame', longitudinal component positive), within the centre distance (rel.centre_distance 'Euclidean ground-plane distance between reference points') at which its lamps engage the approaching driver. rel.centre_distance's exclusion ('Not a stand-in for: a clearance between bodies or an order of arrival') is respected: it only bounds the range of the approach."}, {"span": "t2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "Admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-020::authorized_emergency_vehicle ('a vehicle permitted to depart from certain traffic laws when equipped and operated in the manner provided by law'); ru.aggregate 'membership of a legal aggregate'; its conduct is carried by t4 and t6."}, {"span": "t3", "atoms": ["ru.official_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "ru.official_vehicle 'a vehicle in official or contracted road service ...; kind in {... regulatory_agency ...}', read with kind regulatory_agency; 'Not a stand-in for: an emergency vehicle' respected."}, {"span": "t4", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "sig.hand_signal", "sig.turn_indicator", "rel.visible"], "derived": [], "justification": "'moving': the emergency vehicle's kin.speed above the halt tolerance. 'preparing to move', as t12 defines it, 'any indication that is visible to an approaching driver ... including ... (a) A movement of the vehicle; or (b) The use of hand signals by the driver': sig.hand_signal 'a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning in {no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter}' with a meaning other than no_signal, or sig.turn_indicator 'state in {off, left, right}' other than off (a further visible indication of the open list; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: the turn or lane change itself' respected: it is read as the indication, not the move), with the emergency vehicle visible from the subject (rel.visible 'b is visible from a: an unobstructed line of sight')."}, {"span": "t6", "atoms": ["sig.warning_lamp"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atom only; the span carries gap (t6). sig.warning_lamp 'a warning lamp lit; colour ..., mode ..., facing ...' denotes the lamp, and the quoted requirement 'at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front' needs colour red, mode flashing and facing front; the formula surface reads the atom only by colour and mode, so a lit red flashing lamp of any facing is all a rule can state, a weaker condition than the words; not a stand-in for an audible warning.", "source_spans": ["t7"]}, {"span": "t8", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "Admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'any other' excludes the emergency vehicle itself; 'driver' read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}, {"span": "t9", "atoms": ["dev.human_direction", "dev.governs", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "As the index maps 'except when otherwise directed by a law enforcement officer:' (NRS_484B_267_2e): dev.human_direction ('a person directing traffic'), read with role police_officer, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "t10", "atoms": ["kin.accel_longitudinal", "rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Decrease the speed': kin.accel_longitudinal 'acceleration along heading, signed', at or below minus the deceleration resolution at some observation of the approach before the subject draws level with the emergency vehicle; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: speed' is respected: the decrease is the deceleration, the reached speed is t11's composition. Drawing level: rel.longitudinal_overlap 'the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side)' at or above zero; read only as that projection, as its contract requires."}, {"span": "t12", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "sig.hand_signal", "sig.turn_indicator", "rel.visible"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definition of 'preparing to move' used by t4: 'any indication that is visible to an approaching driver' (rel.visible from the subject to the emergency vehicle) 'that ... is about to move, including, without limitation: (a) A movement of the vehicle' (kin.speed above the halt tolerance) 'or (b) The use of hand signals' (sig.hand_signal other than no_signal); the open list is also read through sig.turn_indicator other than off."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "t7", "as": "definition", "source": "DEF-NRS-484A-480-3", "quote": "at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front"}, {"span": "t11", "rule": "NRS_484B_600_1a", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [{"span": "t5", "why": "illustrative: arriving at or leaving a scene are instances of moving or preparing to move, which t4 already reads; the duty is the same whether or not the vehicle is arriving at or leaving a scene", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "There is a road user e, not the subject, of the authorized-emergency-vehicle aggregate or an official vehicle of kind regulatory_agency, showing a lit warning lamp of colour red, mode flashing, facing front, that is moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) or preparing to move (visible from the subject, rel.visible, with a hand signal other than no_signal or a turn indicator other than off); the subject is approaching e: it moves (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance), e lies ahead of it in its frame (rel.bearing longitudinal positive), their centre distance is at most p.emergency_approach_reach, and they are not side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap negative). And no human_direction device of role police_officer governs a travel region the subject occupies.", "obligation": "(i) The subject complies with NRS_484B_600_1a at this observation (rule composition, subject to subject). (ii) For every such e whose condition rises at this observation (holds here, not at the previous observation): (rel.longitudinal_overlap of the subject and e negative) strong-until (kin.accel_longitudinal of the subject at or below minus p.speed_decrease_decel_min): the subject decelerates before it draws level with e.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.emergency_approach_reach", "p.speed_decrease_decel_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "t8", "why": "'driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "t4", "why": "'preparing to move' is defined (t12) as an indication 'visible to an approaching driver': read as the emergency vehicle being visible from the subject (rel.visible) while it gives the indication", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "perception"}, {"span": "t10", "why": "'decrease the speed' is read as a deceleration beyond the source's resolution at some observation after the approach begins and before the subject draws level; a subject that never draws level and never decelerates leaves this part unknown at the end of the trace", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Ambulance e, moving, with a lit red flashing front lamp, is ahead of the moving subject within p.emergency_approach_reach; the subject holds a constant speed (kin.accel_longitudinal near zero) until its body overlaps e longitudinally."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but the subject decelerates beyond p.speed_decrease_decel_min before drawing level, and its speed meets every bound of NRS_484B_600_1a."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "e's warning lamps are off (no lit sig.warning_lamp) as the subject approaches."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but sig.warning_lamp is not observed, so whether the duty is engaged is unknown.", "masked": ["sig.warning_lamp"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject decelerates before drawing level, but its speed still exceeds the stopping-sight bound of NRS_484B_600_1a on a wet road."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "e stands at rest with its lamps flashing, gives no hand signal and its turn indicator is off: it is neither moving nor preparing to move."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "e stands at rest with lamps flashing and is visible from the subject, its driver giving a hand signal (preparing to move); the subject draws level without decelerating."}, {"name": "branch_4", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "e, moving ahead of the approaching subject, shows red flashing lamps facing only the rear and none facing front: it does not make use of the lamp the borrowed words require."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of the acquisition standard's vehicle-state estimates"}, {"name": "p.emergency_approach_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 150.0, "convention": "centre distance within which a driver approaching an emergency or enforcement vehicle that shows flashing warning lamps counts as approaching it: about the distance at which the lamps are conspicuous by day and a driver at an urban speed of 15 m/s has ten seconds to slow", "source": "emergency warning-light conspicuity studies; move-over law guidance"}, {"name": "p.speed_decrease_decel_min", "unit": "m/s^2", "value": 0.3, "convention": "the longitudinal deceleration at or beyond which a sampled acceleration counts as a decrease of speed rather than noise or rolling resistance: the acceleration resolution of the source", "source": "vehicle-state estimation noise of the acquisition standard"}], "gaps": [{"span": "t6", "kind": "operator", "proposal": "`sig_warning_lamp_facing` [track, colour, mode, facing]: a formula form of the atom sig.warning_lamp that reads the facing attribute its contract already lists (facing in {front, rear, side}) together with colour and mode, true where the road user shows a lit warning lamp of that colour, mode and facing. It decides when the duty arises and toward which approaching vehicles: the condition t6, with the words t7 borrows from DEF-NRS-484A-480-3 ('at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front'), engages the duty to slow only for a vehicle making use of a flashing red lamp facing front. The formula surface reads sig_warning_lamp only as [track, colour] or [track, colour, mode], so a rule can state only a red flashing lamp of any facing, which would engage the duty for a vehicle showing red flashers only to the rear or the side. The same missing form is open as G79-G81, G84 and G85 on the sibling paragraphs of NRS 484B.267.", "nearest": ["sig.warning_lamp: its contract carries colour, mode and facing, but a formula reads only colour and mode; dropping facing weakens a condition span"]}], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_270_2b_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-270-2b"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "When overtaking or passing", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "the driver of a motor vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "shall exercise due care and:", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "If there is only one lane for traffic proceeding in the same direction,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "pass to the left of the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b8", "text": "at a safe distance, which must be not less than 3 feet between any portion of the vehicle and the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "and shall not move again to the right side of the highway", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b10", "text": "until the vehicle is safely clear of the overtaken bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "b11", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in NRS 484B.213 and 484B.217 [NRS-484B-213-1, NRS-484B-213-2a, NRS-484B-213-2b, NRS-484B-213-2c, NRS-484B-217-2],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "b12", "text": "when passing to the left of a bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter at a safe distance of not less than 3 feet between any portion of the vehicle and the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter, this paragraph authorizes the driver, if it is safe, to pass: (1) To the left of the center of the highway. (2) In a no-passing zone.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.overtake_pass"], "justification": "'overtaking or passing' a road user proceeding the same way is drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r): 'a, travelling in the same direction as b, comes from having b ahead of it to having b behind it'; it denotes the relative motion only. The pass is under way while the bodies are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero; a projection, not a contact or a distance), within the window behind the pass's recognition."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a bicycle' is DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'an electric bicycle' DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle, 'an electric scooter' DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor that is designed to be ridden on'); each admitted aggregate claimed whole, as the index maps 'a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter'."}, {"span": "b3", "atoms": ["rel.same_direction", "kin.speed"], "derived": [], "justification": "'proceeding' is the overtaken road user moving (kin.speed above the halt tolerance); 'in the same direction' is rel.same_direction ('headings aligned') between the subject and it, as the index maps 'proceeding in the same direction,'."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a motor vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'). 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b5", "standard": "shall exercise due care", "concepts": ["rel.contact", "kin.accel_longitudinal", "rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "params": ["p.rider_evasive_decel"], "convention": "traffic-conflict technique: the pass is made with due care where the subject's body never touches the overtaken rider's (rel.contact) and the rider is never made to brake harder than an evasive deceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal below its negative) while the two are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero); care is a state of mind, read only through this outcome", "surrogate": true}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_1", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2a", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2b", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_213_2c", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}, {"span": "b11", "rule": "NRS_484B_217_2", "map": {"subject": "subject"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "b12"}], "residues": [{"span": "b12", "why": "the authorization lets a driver passing a rider at the stated clearance pass left of the center or in a no-passing zone, conduct other rules (NRS 484B.213, 484B.217) forbid; it relaxes those rules and leaves the duties of this paragraph unchanged: the duty of care is the same whether or not the authorization holds", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a member of DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle. At the observation, drv.interaction.overtake_pass(subject, r) rises, with window p.overtake_window and same_dir_cos p.overtake_same_direction_cos, for some road user r, not the subject, a member of DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle, DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle or DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter, which at some observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window was moving (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) with its heading aligned with the subject's (rel.same_direction, p.overtake_same_direction_cos). The authorization (b12), suspended where NRS_484B_213_1, NRS_484B_213_2a, NRS_484B_213_2b, NRS_484B_213_2c or NRS_484B_217_2 applies, does not change this duty.", "obligation": "Surrogate. For every such r (re-bound with its whole selection): at every observation of the window behind of length p.overtake_window, the subject is not in contact with r (rel.contact), and wherever the two are side by side (rel.longitudinal_overlap at or above zero) r's longitudinal acceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal) is not below the negative of p.rider_evasive_decel.", "params": ["p.overtake_window", "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.rider_evasive_decel"], "narrowings": [{"span": "b4", "why": "'the driver' of a motor vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "b5", "why": "'due care' is read only through the pass's outcome for the rider: no contact and no evasive braking while side by side; the rule is a surrogate", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a road with one lane in the subject's direction, a bicycle is ridden ahead of the subject car; the subject car overtakes it and its mirror touches the bicyclist while side by side."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same pass, made without contact; the bicyclist keeps its speed."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car overtakes another car; no bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter is in the scene. The duty binds the subject alone."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in permit, but the source does not observe contact between bodies.", "masked": ["rel.contact"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject car overtakes an electric bicycle without touching it, but while they are side by side the rider brakes harder than the evasive deceleration."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.overtake_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of an overtaking manoeuvre on an urban street, from having the overtaken vehicle ahead to having it behind", "source": "overtaking-duration figures"}, {"name": "p.overtake_same_direction_cos", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.9, "convention": "cosine of the largest heading difference (about 25 degrees) at which two vehicles count as travelling in the same direction while one moves out to pass the other", "source": "lane-change heading figures"}, {"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "source speed resolution"}, {"name": "p.rider_evasive_decel", "unit": "m/s^2", "value": 2.0, "convention": "the longitudinal deceleration of a bicycle or scooter rider beyond which its braking counts as an evasive reaction to another road user rather than ordinary speed control: about 0.2 g, above comfortable bicycle braking", "source": "bicycle braking studies; traffic-conflict technique"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
